Closure (Dual Languages)

RDG employs two complementary notions of closure.

The Closure Stability Specification is not the
source of closure.

It is the categorical translation of closure.

The Closure Stability Conjecture is much closer
to the native RDG notion of closure.

(1) Dynamic / Variational Closure
    (Closure Stability Conjecture)

        Γ
        CΓ
        S[x]
        δS = 0
        dΓ

    Closure emerges through dynamical
    organization and variational selection.

(2) Categorical Closure
    (Closure Stability Specification)

        Cl_read

    Closure is represented through
    extensive, idempotent, monotone
    closure operators.

The second serves as a mathematical
representation of the first. The primary
RDG intuition remains the variational
closure picture.
